== binding factor b = f_b + (1 - f_b) <W>  (force on a chi particle from all matter, relative to ungated)
  cosmic f_b (Planck 2018 abstract, Omega_b h^2/(Omega_b h^2 + Omega_c h^2)) = 0.1573
  MW sigma=155: f_b = 0.046 -> b = 0.1516; f_b = 0.100 -> b = 0.1997; f_b = 0.157 -> b = 0.2506
  cluster sigma=1000: f_b = 0.130 -> b = 0.1305; f_b = 0.157 -> b = 0.1578
  (MW f_b = 0.046: stars 5e10 Msun [S: Bland-Hawthorn & Gerhard 2016] + ~1e10 cold gas (dagger) over Mvir 1.3e12 [S, via citing paper])

== crude self-consistency (REDUCED model): chi dispersion set by the force it feels,
   sigma_chi^2 = b(sigma_chi) * sigma_tr^2 (isothermal scaling at fixed density profile), iterate
  MW       f_b = 0.046: sigma_chi =   91.30 km/s (r = 0.761), <W> = 0.3155, b = 0.3470
  MW       f_b = 0.157: sigma_chi =   97.50 km/s (r = 0.813), <W> = 0.2829, b = 0.3957
